{"type":"message","id":"65d9ae60","parentId":"12e3b103","timestamp":"2026-02-12T16:02:10.540Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I will implement a Test-Driven Development (TDD) framework and workflow focusing on creating automated tests to analyze the 'Meta Description' element effectively. Here's my approach:\n\n### Plan for TDD Implementation:\n1. **Understand 'Meta Description' Requirements**:\n   - Determine what attributes a good meta description should have (e.g., length, keyword presence, relevance, uniqueness).\n   - Define edge cases (e.g., overly short/long descriptions, duplication issues, etc.).\n\n2. **Create Automated Tests First:**\n   - Develop unit tests to validate the above attributes of a meta description.\n   - Identify failing scenarios to guide further implementation.\n\n3. **Implement Analysis Logic:**\n   - Develop a function/module that processes user-provided meta descriptions and analyzes them.\n   - Ensure it satisfies the test cases iteratively while adapting to edge cases.\n\n4. **Refine Tests and Functionality:**\n   - Add new tests for regression and emerging corner cases as functionality expands.\n\nI’ll start now with the first set of automated test cases and then build the required core logic."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_WYYkNQEKb8SOdxXuoxo9cVlv","name":"write","arguments":{"path":"ai_meta_description_tests.py","content":"import unittest\n\nclass TestMetaDescriptionAnalysis(unittest.TestCase):\n    \n    def test_meta_description_length(self):\n        \"\"\"Test that meta descriptions meet the length requirements (50-160 characters).\"\"\"\n        description = \"This is a valid meta description with an appropriate length.\"\n        result = analyze_meta_description(description)\n        self.assertTrue(result['is_valid_length'])\n\n    def test_meta_description_too_short(self):\n        \"\"\"Test that overly short meta descriptions are flagged.\"\"\"\n        description = \"Too short.\"\n        result = analyze_meta_description(description)\n        self.assertFalse(result['is_valid_length'])\n\n    def test_meta_description_too_long(self):\n        \"\"\"Test that overly long meta descriptions are flagged.\"\"\"\n        description = \"This is an overly long meta description. \" * 10\n        result = analyze_meta_description(description)\n        self.assertFalse(result['is_valid_length'])\n\n    def test_meta_description_keyword_presence(self):\n        \"\"\"Test that a keyword is present in the meta description.\"\"\"\n        description = \"Learn Python programming with this detailed tutorial.\"\n        keyword = \"Python\"\n        result = analyze_meta_description(description, keyword)\n        self.assertTrue(result['contains_keyword'])\n\n    def test_meta_description_missing_keyword(self):\n        \"\"\"Test meta descriptions without the provided keyword.\"\"\"\n        description = \"Learn programming with this detailed tutorial.\"\n        keyword = \"Python\"\n        result = analyze_meta_description(description, keyword)\n        self.assertFalse(result['contains_keyword'])\n\n    def test_meta_description_uniqueness(self):\n        \"\"\"Test that the meta description is unique compared to others.\"\"\"\n        description = \"Unique meta description for the page.\"\n        existing_descriptions = [\n            \"Generic meta description for another page.\",\n            \"Some generic description for a different page.\"\n        ]\n        result = analyze_meta_description(description, existing_descriptions=existing_descriptions)\n        self.assertTrue(result['is_unique'])\n\n    def test_meta_description_not_unique(self):\n        \"\"\"Test that duplicate meta descriptions are flagged.\"\"\"\n        description = \"Duplicate meta description.\"\n        existing_descriptions = [\n            \"Duplicate meta description.\",\n            \"Some other description for a different page.\"\n        ]\n        result = analyze_meta_description(description, existing_descriptions=existing_descriptions)\n        self.assertFalse(result['is_unique'])\n\n# Placeholder for the actual analysis function to implement the TDD approach.\ndef analyze_meta_description(description, keyword=None, existing_descriptions=None):\n    return {\n        'is_valid_length': False,\n        'contains_keyword': False,\n        'is_unique': False\n    }\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    unittest.main()"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"github-copilot","model":"gpt-4o","usage":{"input":6077,"output":881,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":6958,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1770912120597}}
